p95 latency spiked to 1.2 s on Sept 2 during the payment provider outage, then returned to 240 ms. Availability 99.71%, below the 99.9% SLO."}],"metadata":{"service":"checkout-api","week":"2026-W36","week_start":"2026-08-31","week_end":"2026-09-06","title":"checkout-api weekly SLO report, week 36"},"raw_score":1.2234247312429805,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c4","rank":1},{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c5","rank":1}]},"score":0.099974,"p_relevant":0.0,"rationale":"Checkout dashboard","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"INC-4915","source":"incidents","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"auth-gateway elevated latency\n\nauth-gateway p95 latency doubled to 220 ms for an hour because of a noisy neighbour on the shared Redis. Moved session reads to the dedicated cluster."}],"metadata":{"opened":"2026-10-09","service":"auth-gateway","severity":"SEV3","status":"resolved","title":"auth-gateway elevated latency"},"raw_score":2.091746326918598,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c0","rank":1},{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c1","rank":2}]},"score":0.099181,"p_relevant":0.0,"rationale":"Unrelated auth gateway incident","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"INC-4584","source":"incidents","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Order confirmation emails delayed\n\nConfirmation emails arrived up to 2 hours late. The email vendor throttled us after a bounce spike. Vendor lifted the limit."}],"metadata":{"opened":"2026-07-11","service":"notify-svc","severity":"SEV3","status":"resolved","title":"Order confirmation emails delayed"},"raw_score":3.3927134582185787,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c0","rank":0},{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c1","rank":5}]},"score":0.097764,"p_relevant":0.0,"rationale":"Unrelated email incident","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"INC-4821","source":"incidents","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"search-api p95 elevated across all regions\n\nOpened by on-call (Priya Raman) at 09:12 UTC after the SLO burn alert fired. search-api p95 latency climbed from ~180 ms to ~640 ms starting early Sept 14 and is holding there. p50 is only slightly up. Error rate is flat, so requests succeed but slowly. CPU on the search-api pods is up ~35%. Checked the CDN and the edge cache: both look normal. No config pushes in the last 12 hours. Mitigation so far: scaled search-api from 24 to 36 pods, which took p95 down to ~520 ms but did not clear it. Root cause: not yet identified. Leaving open for the search team to investigate on Monday. Customer impact: slower search results pages, some timeouts on the mobile app's type-ahead."}],"metadata":{"opened":"2026-09-14","service":"search-api","severity":"SEV2","status":"resolved","title":"search-api p95 elevated across all regions"},"raw_score":0.6489217206265213,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c0","rank":5},{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c1","rank":1}]},"score":0.096944,"p_relevant":0.0,"rationale":"Search latency incident in September, mentions search-api p95 elevated.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"INC-4710","source":"incidents","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Search results slow for EU shoppers\n\nCustomers in the EU reported slow search pages from 14:00 UTC. search-api p95 latency rose to ~900 ms for EU traffic only. Traced to a CDN configuration change that removed the regional cache rule for /search, so every request went to origin. Rolled back the CDN change at 15:40 UTC and p95 returned to normal within 10 minutes. Root cause: CDN config change (change ticket CHG-2231). Follow-up: add the cache rule to the CDN config tests."}],"metadata":{"opened":"2026-08-21","service":"search-api","severity":"SEV2","status":"resolved","title":"Search results slow for EU shoppers"},"raw_score":0.8840543349832302,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c0","rank":4},{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c1","rank":3}]},"score":0.096105,"p_relevant":0.0,"rationale":"Unrelated CDN incident","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"INC-4762","source":"incidents","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Payment provider outage\n\nThe card payment provider h